      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first courthouse was a log building, replaced by the current brick courthouse built in the late 19th century at the same spot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomfield%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bloomfield’s Vitrified Brick and Tile Factory, operating from 1908 to the 1980s, supplied bricks for historic Indianapolis structures like Victory Field.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://getindiana.com/news/bloomfield",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Tulip Trestle, standing 157 feet tall and stretching 2,300 feet, is America’s longest railroad trestle and still serves the Indiana Railroad Company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
